les.  \nFrom Section&nbsp;3 we have proved that no tiling can use fewer than \\(2n-2\\) tiles.  \nTherefore the minimum possible number of tiles equals \\(2n-2\\).\n\nFor the given grid \\(n=2025\\),\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\cdot2025-2=4048}\n\\]\n\ntiles are necessary and sufficient.  \n\n∎"
